# PROBE disjoint-binary. A ⊑ B, A ⊑ C and B disjoint C make A unsatisfiable; B and C stay satisfiable.
# construct: DisjointClasses
# expect: unsat :A
# expect-not: unsat :B
# expect-not: unsat :C

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B , :C .
:B owl:disjointWith :C .
